Q: Check Error Count Angular Reactive Forms A: <p>This recursive function will also count nested errors:</p>
<pre><code>const countFormErrors = (control: AbstractControl): number =&gt; {
    if (control instanceof FormGroup) {
        return Object.keys(control.controls)
            .reduce((acc, key) =&gt; acc + countFormErrors(control.controls[key]), 0);
    }

    if (control instanceof FormArray) {
        return control.controls
            .reduce((acc, arrayControl) =&gt; acc + countFormErrors(arrayControl), 0);
    }

    return control.invalid ? 1 : 0;
}

const formErrorCount = countFormErrors(this.form);
</code></pre>

Q: :after pseudo not taking direction (rtl) in consideration? (Firefox) A: <p>I know it is a very old question but I also faced the same problem and, in my case, I could not use <code>display: inline-block</code> as suggested by the <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/8712310/12124759">accepted answer</a>.</p>
<p>The pseudo elements <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::before" rel="nofollow noreferrer">::before</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::after" rel="nofollow noreferrer">::after</a> seem to follow the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/direction" rel="nofollow noreferrer">direction</a> if the content is not blank or empty, so another solution is to add a non breaking space with <code>content: &quot;\00A0&quot;</code> and change its width if needed with <code>letter-spacing</code>.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>div::before {
  content: "\00A0";
  margin: 5px;
  letter-spacing: 10px;
  background: red;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div dir="ltr"&gt;Left to right&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div dir="rtl"&gt;Right to left&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Which PATH variable do I need to specify in execve() in order to launch my program? A: <p>The <code>path</code> parameter isn't for passing the PATH environment variable.  It's for passing the path to your program.</p>
<p>For example, if your program resides as /path/to/program and you want to pass it &quot;aa&quot;, &quot;bb&quot;, and &quot;cc&quot; as parameters, you would call <code>execve</code> as follows:</p>
<pre><code>char *args[] = {&quot;program_name&quot;, &quot;aa&quot;, &quot;bb&quot;, &quot;cc&quot;, NULL};
execve(&quot;/path/to/program&quot;, args, NULL);
// if you get here, execve failed
perror(&quot;execve failed&quot;);
</code></pre>

Q: CSS won&#39;t align &lt;li&gt; A: <p>I would suggest you to use
<strong><a href="https://css-tricks.com/snippets/css/a-guide-to-flexbox/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">flexbox</a></strong> on both
your <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> elements. This will give you much more control on alignment, spacing, etc. It may also simplify your media queries, for changing the layout on
smaller screens.</p>
<p>Also, a few other improvements I propose:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Use CSS properties (variables), to simplify future changes by putting them all at
the top of your CSS.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Use the <code>border-box</code>
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/box-sizing" rel="nofollow noreferrer">box sizing</a>
model to simplify things a lot.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Avoid setting font size in <code>px</code> unit, but put this on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> (or <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>)
tag and then use the <code>em</code> or <code>rem</code> unit. This way, if you want to decrease or
increase the font size for all the page, you just have one single place to do it.</p>
<p>Here, I used the <code>clamp()</code> CSS function to say that the font size should be 3% of
the viewport width, but with a minimum of <code>1em</code> (16px, set on <code>html</code>) and a max
of <code>2em</code> (2 x 16px = 32px).</p>
</li>
<li><p>Use CSS functions to manipulate colors. This way, you can decline some colors,
based on your theme colors, without having to create many color variables.</p>
</li>
<li><p>About the logo: the <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> attributes of an image do not
contain an unit. It is always pixels. You may have seen this in the <code>style</code>
attribute, containing CSS rules with units.</p>
<p>You also have to set the mandatory <code>alt</code> attribute.</p>
<p>Usually, the logo is also a link pointing to the homepage URL, so I suggest
that you also do that, in order to help your visitors.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Keep your menu links in lowercase with the first letter in uppercase inside
the HTML source code. Then use CSS to do the uppercase rendering.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>:root {
  --html-font-size: 16px;
  --html-line-height: 1.4;
  --html-font-family: Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif;

  --header-bg-color: #304852;
  --header-text-color: white;
  --header-link-color: white; /* Same color as text? Not confusing? */
  --header-link-hover-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--header-text-color) 80%, blue);
  --header-border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--header-bg-color), black);
}

html {
  font: var(--html-font-size)/var(--html-line-height) var(--html-font-family);
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

*, *::before, *::after {
  box-sizing: inherit;
}

header {
  background: var(--header-bg-color);
  color: var(--header-text-color);
  border-bottom: 3px solid var(--header-border-color);
  display: flex;       /* By default will be horizontal. */
  align-items: center; /* Align vertically with the logo. */
}

#logo img {
  display: block; /* Remove the stupid bottom spacing. */
}

header a,
header a:link,
header a:visited {
  color: var(--header-link-color);
  text-decoration: none;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  /* Make font size 3% of the viewport width, with limits. */
  font-size: clamp(1em, 3vw, 2em);
}
header a:hover,
header a:active {
  color: var(--header-link-hover-color);
}

header nav ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;    /* By default will be horizontal. */
  list-style: none; /* Remove the bullet points. */
}

header nav li {
  padding: 0 0 0 2em;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;header&gt;
  &lt;div id="logo"&gt;
    &lt;img src="https://picsum.photos/120/60/"
         width="120" height="60" alt="Logo of the company"&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;nav&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#home"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#about"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#blog"&gt;Blog&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#contact"&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
  &lt;/nav&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
